Emit torch::kBFloat16 for BFloat16 tensor element type (shader-slang/slang#11040).

Source change from upstream commit 7c1bfb7f2, on top of v2026.4 (which predates
it). Without it, TensorView<BFloat16> aborts -target torch-binding with "error
99999: unknown scalar type". Emitter fix only, tests omitted.

Modified by NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES, 2026 (statement of changes, Apache-2.0
section 4(b)): this patch changes source/slang/slang-emit-torch.cpp of Slang v2026.4.

diff --git a/source/slang/slang-emit-torch.cpp b/source/slang/slang-emit-torch.cpp
--- a/source/slang/slang-emit-torch.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-emit-torch.cpp
@@ -31,6 +31,9 @@ void emitTorchScalarTypeName(SourceWriter* m_writer, IRInst* type)
     case kIROp_HalfType:
         m_writer->emit("kFloat16");
         break;
+    case kIROp_BFloat16Type:
+        m_writer->emit("kBFloat16");
+        break;
     case kIROp_DoubleType:
         m_writer->emit("kFloat64");
         break;
